{"file_path":"build_memo.py","old_string":"(c) Within forty-five (45) days following the end of the Earnout Period, Buyer shall prepare and deliver to Seller a written statement (the “Earnout Statement”) setting forth Buyer’s good-faith calculation of Adjusted EBITDA for the Earnout Period and the resulting Earnout Payment, if any, together with reasonable supporting detail. Seller shall have thirty (30) days following receipt of the Earnout Statement to review the Earnout Statement and deliver a written notice of objection specifying in reasonable detail each disputed item and the amount Seller believes to be correct. Any dispute not resolved by the Parties within twenty (20) Business Days after delivery of such notice shall be submitted to the Independent Accountant under Section 2.04(c), whose determination shall be final and binding absent manifest error.

(d) Following the Closing, Buyer shall not, and shall cause the Company not to, take any action with the primary purpose of avoiding or reducing the Earnout Payment.","new_string":"(c) Within forty-five (45) days following the end of the Earnout Period, Buyer shall prepare and deliver to Seller a written statement (the “Earnout Statement”) setting forth Buyer’s good-faith calculation of Adjusted EBITDA for the Earnout Period and the resulting Earnout Payment, if any, together with reasonable supporting detail. Seller shall have thirty (30) days following receipt of the Earnout Statement to review the Earnout Statement and deliver a written notice of objection specifying in reasonable detail each disputed item and the amount Seller believes to be correct. Buyer shall pay any undisputed Earnout Payment within sixty (60) days following the end of the Earnout Period. Any dispute not resolved by the Parties within twenty (20) Business Days after delivery of such notice shall be submitted to the Independent Accountant under Section 2.04(c), whose determination shall be final and binding absent manifest error, and any additional amount determined to be payable shall be paid within five (5) Business Days after such final determination.

(d) Following the Closing, Buyer shall not, and shall cause the Company not to, take any action with the primary purpose of avoiding or reducing the Earnout Payment."}

